WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.500
This covers what changed since the last film.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:11.800
One new crate. It is how the application talks to the model.

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.800
Every fact in a report comes back through this function.

4
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:23.800
The schema is built from the Rust type you asked for.

5
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:30.000
So changing the type changes what the model may produce, in the same commit.

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.600
This is the test that had to pass before anything else was built.

7
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:43.500
A hundred generations. Every one parsed. None had the wrong contents.

8
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:49.700
The enum is the point: nothing else stops a model returning a fourth option.

9
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:55.700
The same run found something less welcome.

10
00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:02.900
Eleven seconds for one extraction, on a machine faster than the real one.

11
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:09.000
It is written down as a problem rather than left under the passing result.

12
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.200
This test needs a model server. The build machine has none.

13
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:22.800
So it skips and says why, unless something tells it the server should be there.

14
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:28.800
The checks that run on every change.

15
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:35.700
Including a build for the Arm chip the service will actually run on.

16
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.900
The model path works. How long it takes is the open question.
